Thanks for the fix, although you probably dislike it as much as I do.

The problem seems to be in the only setIs() remaining in sp; if I modify
it to spitting debug prints by:

setIs("SpatialGrid", "SpatialPixels",
    coerce = function(from) {
        print("coercing by setIs() on SpatialGrid")
        SpatialPixels(SpatialPoints(coordinates(from), from at proj4string),
        grid = from at grid)
        },
    replace = function(from, value) stop("replace-coercion not allowed")
)

then testing on test.ag in inst/external gives:

> x = readGDAL("test.ag")
test.ag has GDAL driver AAIGrid
and has 115 rows and 80 columns
[1] "coercing by setIs() on SpatialGrid"
[1] "coercing by setIs() on SpatialGrid"

So, apparently, setIs() causes the validity checking of SpatialGrid or
SpatialGridDataFrame to ALSO coerce to SpatialPixels[DataFrame], not
only once but twice, to check validity there. Indeed, a pretty stupid
thing to do.

maybe it should be setIs("SpatialPixels", "SpatialGrid", ...) ?

will look into this; would be good to have this settled before 1.0, it
has given me a few headaches before, see

http://lists.r-forge.r-project.org/pipermail/rspatial-devel/2011-September/000023.html

